@startuml
!include style.iuml
' PDF report: ReportsPage -> POST /api/analytics/exams/{examId}/report (AnalyticsController, Roles
' Admin,SuperAdmin,Teacher), ExamAccessService.DenyUnlessAsync(Owner), AnalyticsService.GetExamSummaryAsync
' + GenerateExamReportPdfAsync (QuestPDF; file in Reports/, row in ExamReports), GET /api/analytics/exams/{examId}/reports,
' GET /api/analytics/reports/{fileName} (bare name 400, no row 404, not owner 403, file missing 404). The summary PDF is
' not audited; the Module 12 exports (POST /api/analytics/reports/{type}) are audited as REPORT_GENERATED with the
' file's SHA-256 (ReportExportService).
' Simplified labels: endpoints, status codes and file details are in the chapter text.
' Large font at dpi 96. Printed pt = fontSize * printed_width_pt / png_width_px.
skinparam dpi 96
skinparam defaultFontSize 28
skinparam ArrowFontSize 27
skinparam padding 1
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #777777
  TitleFontSize 29
}
|Staff (ReportsPage)|
start
:Select an exam,
click Generate
New Report;
|Server|
if (Exam exists, caller\nowner or admin?) then ([no])
  :Refuse;
  stop
else ([yes])
endif
:Compute summary: marks,
score buckets, question
averages, violations;
:Build PDF: summary,
per-question results,
score distribution;
:Save file, record it,
return a link;
note right
  Not audited. Other
  exports are audited
  with a SHA-256 hash.
end note
|Staff (ReportsPage)|
:Reload history,
click Download;
|Server|
if (Valid name, known\nreport, owner or admin?) then ([yes])
  :Return
  the PDF;
else ([no])
  :Refuse;
endif
stop
@enduml
